    {
      "id": "05-04",
      "title": "Routing versus forwarding",
      "chapter": "The routing puzzle",
      "duration": 21.166666666666668,
      "narration": "Before calculating, separate routing from forwarding. Routing builds the choices; forwarding uses them to move a packet to its next hop. A packet can follow an established choice without running a new shortest-path calculation at every arrival.",
      "bullets": [
        "Routing builds the choices",
        "Forwarding uses those choices"
      ],
      "takeaway": "Compute routes in the control plane; forward packets using the result.",
